Subject: Run krdpserver from the settings page when no systemd user manager is on the session bus

The Remote Desktop page starts, stops, enables and reads krdpserver only
through org.freedesktop.systemd1, so without systemd it hides its switch
and says the server needs manual activation. krdpserver now owns a
unique D-Bus name through KDBusService (org.kde.krdp-server), and when
systemd1 is absent the page starts the program itself, stops it through
that name's /MainApplication quit, reads its state from the name, and
turns "start at login" into an autostart entry, a copy of
org.kde.krdpserver.desktop in the user's autostart folder. With systemd
nothing changes.

